<title>USA: Delaware session ending with bond, budget votes.</title>
<headline>Delaware session ending with bond, budget votes.</headline>
<dateline>DOVER, Del. 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delaware's 1997 legislative session is set to end Monday with approval expected on next year's budget and bonding bills.</p>
<p>Republican Roger Roy said the state's bond bill amounts to more than $350 million, part of which will cover Delaware's six-year transportation budget.</p>
<p>The voting session is expected to last into the early morning hours.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
